    <bpmn:process id="W_W1306" name="W1306. Multi-Entity Statutory Benefits Consolidation, Remittance Reconciliation &amp; Government Portal Compliance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly statutory benefits remittance deadline (SSS: last day of month; PhilHealth: every 10th; Pag-IBIG: every 10th of following month); or quarterly reconciliation cycle
Frequency: Monthly remittance across 5 entities (15 separate filings/month: 5 entities × 3 agencies); quarterly reconciliation
Volume: 6,911 employees across 5 entities; ~PHP 100–120M/month in total statutory contributions (employee + employer share)
Owner: Payroll Manager
Participants: Payroll Manager, Payroll Analyst, HR Data Specialist, Finance Controller, SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG branch representatives
Source: workflow W1306 — Multi-Entity Statutory Benefits Consolidation, Remittance Reconciliation &amp; Government Portal Compliance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1306_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1306_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1306_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1306_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1306_Lane2" name="Payroll Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1306_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1306_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1306_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1306_Lane3" name="Payroll Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1306_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1306_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1306_Start5" name="Monthly statutory benefits remittance deadline (SSS: last day of month; PhilHealth: every…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1306_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1306_Task6" name="Monthly contribution calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly contribution calculation: (a) upon completion of semi-monthly payroll runs per entity (W10), system calculates statutory contributions per employee: (i) SSS: monthly salary credit determination (based on actual monthly compensation, mapped to SSS salary bracket), employer and employee share calculation; (ii) PhilHealth: monthly basic salary (capped at PHP 80,000), employer and employee share at 2.5% each; (iii) Pag-IBIG: monthly basic salary (capped at PHP 5,000 for mandatory contributions), employer and employee share at 2% each; (b) system generates contribution schedule per entity: (i) employee-level breakdown: employee ID, name, SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG number, monthly salary, employer share, employee share, total; (ii) entity-level summary: total employer contribution, total employee contribution (deducted from payroll), grand total remittance per agency; (c) Payroll Analyst reviews calculated contributions: (i) verify no employee has missing SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG number (new hires must be registered per W518), (ii) verify salary caps applied correctly, (iii) verify employee on leave without pay excluded from contribution for the period
Responsible (R): System / Payroll Analyst
Accountable (A): Payroll Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1306_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1306_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1306_Task7" name="Monthly remittance filing &amp; payment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Monthly remittance filing &amp; payment: (a) Payroll Analyst generates remittance files per entity per agency: (i) SSS: generate R3 (Contributions Collection List) file in SSS format → upload to SSS online portal → obtain PRN → process payment via BDO/BPI online banking before month-end deadline; (ii) PhilHealth: generate ER2 (Premium Remittance) file in PhilHealth EPRS format → upload to PhilHealth portal → process payment before 10th of following month; (iii) Pag-IBIG: generate Member&#x27;s Contribution Form (MCF) file in Pag-IBIG format → upload to Pag-IBIG online portal → process payment before 14th of following month; (b) for each entity: 3 separate filings × 5 entities = 15 filings/month; (c) payment released from each entity&#x27;s designated bank account (not commingled — BuildRight Depot&#x27;s SSS payment comes from Depot&#x27;s bank account, not Holdings&#x27; account)
Responsible (R): Payroll Analyst
Accountable (A): Payroll Manager
Duration: 4–6 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1306_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1306_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1306_Task8" name="Remittance reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Remittance reconciliation: (a) after payment confirmation from bank: Payroll Analyst reconciles each remittance: (i) bank debit amount matches system-calculated remittance amount, (ii) SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG portal shows payment posted to correct employer number and correct billing period, (iii) employee-level contributions posted correctly to individual member records; (b) common discrepancies: (i) PRN expired (SSS PRNs are valid for the billing month only — late payment requires new PRN generation with penalties), (ii) employee SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG number mismatch (employee transferred between entities but membership record not updated), (iii) over/under payment due to payroll adjustment (late overtime inclusion, retroactive salary increase) — requires supplementary remittance; (c) resolve all discrepancies within 5 business days of remittance
Responsible (R): Payroll Analyst
Accountable (A): Payroll Manager
Duration: 3–4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1306_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1306_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1306_Task9" name="Quarterly reconciliation &amp; government portal audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quarterly reconciliation &amp; government portal audit: (a) quarterly, Payroll Manager reconciles cumulative statutory contributions: (i) total payroll deductions (employee share) per GL account vs. total remittances to each agency — any difference indicates unremitted deductions (serious DOLE violation) or over-remittance; (ii) employee count per entity per agency vs. active employee count per HR system — discrepancies indicate unregistered new hires or unreported separations; (iii) download employee contribution records from SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG portals and compare to internal records — verify all employee contributions posted correctly; (b) for any unreconciled items: investigate and resolve — common causes: late new-hire registration (SSS number application takes 2–4 weeks for new employees), returned payments (wrong employer number, wrong billing period)
Responsible (R): Payroll Manager / Payroll Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1306_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1306_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1306_Task10" name="Employee benefit claim support">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Employee benefit claim support: (a) when an employee files for SSS sickness/maternity/disability/retirement benefit, PhilHealth hospitalization claim, or Pag-IBIG housing loan/calamity loan: Payroll Analyst provides supporting documentation: (i) certificate of employment with compensation history, (ii) contribution history printout from ERP, (iii) employer certification of contributions remitted; (b) for maternity benefit (105 days under RA 11210 / Expanded Maternity Leave): Payroll Analyst processes: (i) advance maternity payment to employee per W10 (off-cycle payment if needed per W641), (ii) SSS maternity reimbursement claim on behalf of employee, (iii) SSS reimbursement received and reconciled per entity
Responsible (R): Payroll Analyst
Accountable (A): Payroll Manager
Duration: Per claim: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1306_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1306_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1306_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1306_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1306_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-297 (ensure controlled execution — Payroll &amp; Compensation (PA-19.2).) | - operational: Payroll Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Payroll Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1306_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1306_Annotation12" targetRef="W1306_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1306_Flow14" sourceRef="W1306_Start5" targetRef="W1306_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1306_Flow15" sourceRef="W1306_Task6" targetRef="W1306_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1306_Flow16" sourceRef="W1306_Task7" targetRef="W1306_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1306_Flow17" sourceRef="W1306_Task8" targetRef="W1306_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1306_Flow18" sourceRef="W1306_Task9" targetRef="W1306_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1306_Flow19" sourceRef="W1306_Task10" targetRef="W1306_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1306_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1306_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1306">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1306_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1306_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1306_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1306_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1306_Lane3_di" bpmnElement="W1306_Lane3" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="420" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1306_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1306_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1306_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1306_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1306_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1306_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1306_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W1306_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="465" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1306_Task10_di" bpmnElement="W1306_Task10"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1306_Start5_di" bpmnElement="W1306_Start5"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1306_End11_di" bpmnElement="W1306_End11"><dc:Bounds x="1470" y="487" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1306_Annotation12_di" bpmnElement="W1306_Annotation12"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="630" width="360" height="72" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1306_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W1306_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1306_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1306_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1306_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1306_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="790" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1306_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W1306_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1306_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W1306_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="505" /><di:waypoint x="1240" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1306_Flow19_di" bpmnElement="W1306_Flow19"><di:waypoint x="1420" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1470" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1306_Assoc13_di" bpmnElement="W1306_Assoc13"><di:waypoint x="340" y="630" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1416" name="W1416. Philippine 13th Month Pay Computation, Monthly Accrual Booking &amp; Year-End Compliance Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly accrual cycle (ongoing); year-end payment processing (November–December); or employee separation (W643) triggering pro-rated 13th month payout
Frequency: Monthly accrual; annual computation and payment (paid by December 24 per Presidential Decree No. 851)
Volume: 6,911 employees across 5 legal entities; ~1,200–1,600 separations/year requiring pro-rated computation
Owner: Payroll Manager
Participants: Payroll Manager, HR Specialist, Controller, FP&amp;A Analyst, DOLE Compliance Officer
Source: workflow W1416 — Philippine 13th Month Pay Computation, Monthly Accrual Booking &amp; Year-End Compliance Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1416_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1416_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1416_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1416_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1416_Lane2" name="Payroll Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1416_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1416_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1416_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1416_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1416_Lane3" name="HR Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1416_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1416_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1416_Start5" name="Monthly accrual cycle (ongoing); year-end payment processing (November–December); or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1416_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1416_Task6" name="Monthly accrual booking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly accrual booking: Each payroll run (semi-monthly), Payroll Manager books 13th month accrual: (a) accrual = total basic salary for the pay period ÷ 12, (b) journal entry: Dr. 13th Month Pay Expense / Cr. 13th Month Pay Accrued Liability, (c) accrual posted per entity (5 entities × 2 payroll runs/month = 10 journal entries/month), (d) FP&amp;A Analyst reviews monthly accrual vs. budget
Responsible (R): System / Payroll Manager
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: Automated per payroll run</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1416_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1416_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1416_Task7" name="Quarterly accrual reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Quarterly accrual reconciliation: Quarterly, Payroll Manager reconciles: (a) accumulated 13th month accrual balance per GL vs. sum of individual employee accruals from payroll system, (b) identify discrepancies: employees transferred between entities (accrual must transfer), employees on leave without pay (accrual should reduce), new hires (accrual should start from hire date), separated employees (accrual should have been paid with final pay), (c) post adjustments as needed
Responsible (R): Payroll Manager
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2–4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1416_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1416_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1416_Task8" name="Mid-year computation preview">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Mid-year computation preview (June): Payroll Manager generates mid-year 13th month projection: (a) per-employee projected 13th month pay based on current salary rate × 12 months (or pro-rated for partial year), (b) total projected liability per entity and consolidated, (c) compare to current accrual balance: identify any shortfall or over-accrual, (d) FP&amp;A Analyst incorporates into mid-year cash flow forecast per W37 (treasury cash forecasting)
Responsible (R): Payroll Manager / FP&amp;A Analyst
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4–6 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1416_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1416_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1416_Task9" name="Year-end computation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Year-end computation (November): Payroll Manager runs final 13th month computation: (a) per-employee computation: total basic salary earned Jan 1 – Dec 31 ÷ 12 = 13th month pay, (b) adjustments for: (i) leaves without pay (basic salary reduced by unpaid leave days), (ii) salary changes during the year (each salary period computed separately then summed), (iii) mid-year hires (pro-rated from hire date), (iv) employees who received 13th month advance or partial payment during the year, (c) tax computation: 13th month pay up to PHP 90,000 is tax-exempt; any amount above PHP 90,000 is added to December taxable income and taxed per graduated rates
Responsible (R): Payroll Manager
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1416_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1416_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1416_Task10" name="Payment processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Payment processing (by December 24): (a) Payroll Manager submits 13th month payment batch to bank: typically paid with the December 15 or December 30 payroll run, (b) for each entity: generate payment file, Controller approves, Treasury releases payment per W34, (c) system posts: Dr. 13th Month Pay Accrued Liability / Cr. Cash (Bank), (d) any remaining accrual balance closed to expense (for employees who separated during the year but accrual was retained)
Responsible (R): Payroll Manager / Treasury
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4–6 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1416_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1416_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1416_Task11" name="DOLE compliance documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: DOLE compliance documentation: (a) Payroll Manager maintains 13th month pay records per DOLE requirements: (i) employee name, (ii) basic salary per month, (iii) total basic salary earned, (iv) 13th month pay amount, (v) date paid, (b) records must be available for DOLE inspection per W54 (regulatory compliance), (c) employee acknowledgment of receipt filed per entity
Responsible (R): HR Specialist / Payroll Manager
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 2–4 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1416_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1416_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1416_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1416_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1416_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-297 (ensure controlled execution — Payroll &amp; Compensation (PA-19.2).) | - operational: monthly accrual booking and mid-year projection for treasury planning per W37
Owner: Payroll Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1416_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1416_Annotation13" targetRef="W1416_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
