    <bpmn:process id="W_W1527" name="W1527. Employee SSS, PhilHealth, Pag-IBIG Monthly Contribution Filing, Remittance &amp; Reconciliation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Semi-monthly payroll processing cycle (15th and 30th pay periods)
Frequency: Monthly filing and remittance (contributions deducted from payroll must be remitted to each agency by specified deadlines: SSS by last day of following month, PhilHealth by end of following month, Pag-IBIG by 10th of following month)
Volume: ~6,911 employees across 5 legal entities (200 stores + 4 DCs + HQ)
Owner: Payroll Manager
Participants: Payroll Manager, Payroll Clerks, HR Business Partner, Finance Controller, SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG portal administrators
Source: workflow W1527 — Employee SSS, PhilHealth, Pag-IBIG Monthly Contribution Filing, Remittance &amp; Reconciliation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1527_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1527_Lane1" name="Payroll Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1527_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1527_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1527_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1527_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1527_Lane2" name="HR Business Partner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1527_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1527_Lane3" name="Payroll Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1527_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1527_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1527_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1527_Start5" name="Semi-monthly payroll processing cycle (15th and 30th pay periods)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1527_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1527_Task6" name="Payroll deduction computation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Payroll deduction computation (semi-monthly): (a) during payroll processing per W644/1416: Payroll Clerk runs statutory benefits computation: (i) SSS: employee share (4.5% of MSC) and employer share (9.5% of MSC) based on SSS contribution table (tiered by monthly salary credit — 2026 rates); (ii) PhilHealth: employee share (2.5%) and employer share (2.5%) based on monthly basic salary (floor: PHP 10,000, ceiling: PHP 80,000); (iii) Pag-IBIG: employee share (1% or 2% based on monthly compensation) and employer share (2%); (b) system auto-calculates per employee based on: salary, employment status (regular, probationary, seasonal/project — seasonal workers also covered), entity assignment; (c) total deductions per employee reflected on payslip
Responsible (R): Payroll Clerk / System
Accountable (A): Payroll Manager
Duration: Automated during payroll run</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1527_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1527_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1527_Task7" name="Monthly contribution report generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Monthly contribution report generation: (a) after both semi-monthly payrolls processed (end of month): system generates monthly contribution reports for each agency and each legal entity: (i) SSS Form R-3 (Contribution Collection List): employee names, SSS numbers, MSC, employee share, employer share, total per employee; (ii) PhilHealth ERP (Electronic Premium Remittance) file: employee PhilHealth numbers, monthly basic salary, employee share, employer share; (iii) Pag-IBIG MCR (Member&#x27;s Contribution Remittance) form: employee Pag-IBIG numbers, monthly compensation, employee share, employer share; (b) Payroll Clerk reviews reports for anomalies: (i) new hires without SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG numbers, (ii) separated employees still appearing in report, (iii) unusually high or low contribution amounts
Responsible (R): Payroll Clerk / System
Accountable (A): Payroll Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours per agency per entity = ~15–20 hours total</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1527_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1527_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1527_Task8" name="New hire registration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: New hire registration (if needed): (a) for employees without SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG numbers (typically new hires who are first-time workers): (i) HR Business Partner registers employee online via each agency&#x27;s portal (SSS online registration, PhilHealth electronic registration, Pag-IBIG online membership); (ii) registration typically takes 3–5 business days for number generation; (b) Payroll Clerk flags unregistered employees in contribution report; contributions for unregistered employees are accumulated and remitted retroactively once numbers are issued
Responsible (R): HR Business Partner / Payroll Clerk
Accountable (A): Payroll Manager
Duration: 15–20 min per new hire</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1527_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1527_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1527_Task9" name="Remittance payment processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Remittance payment processing: (a) Payroll Manager authorizes payment to each agency for each entity: (i) SSS: via SSS online payment facility or accredited bank (BDO, Metrobank, etc.); total remittance = employer share + employee share deductions across all employees in entity; (ii) PhilHealth: via PhilHealth electronic remittance or accredited bank; (iii) Pag-IBIG: via Pag-IBIG online payment or accredited collecting partner; (b) Finance Controller reviews and approves fund transfers from each entity&#x27;s bank account; (c) payments made by deadline: SSS (last day of following month), PhilHealth (end of following month), Pag-IBIG (10th of following month)
Responsible (R): Payroll Manager / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 hours per entity × 5 entities = ~10–15 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1527_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1527_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1527_Task10" name="Reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Reconciliation: (a) Payroll Clerk reconciles: (i) total deductions in payroll system vs. total remitted to each agency (must match to the peso); (ii) per-employee contributions in payroll system vs. per-employee contributions in agency reports; (b) common discrepancies: (i) late new-hire registration causes retroactive adjustment, (ii) mid-month separation causes proration, (iii) salary adjustment effective mid-month causes split contribution; (c) Payroll Clerk resolves discrepancies and files adjusted report with agency if needed
Responsible (R): Payroll Clerk
Accountable (A): Payroll Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours per entity per month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1527_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1527_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1527_Task11" name="Quarterly audit and employee statement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quarterly audit and employee statement: (a) quarterly: Payroll Manager reviews cumulative contributions per employee across all 3 agencies: (i) YTD employee share vs. expected based on YTD salary, (ii) any employees with contribution gaps (unpaid leaves, LWOP exceeding 1 month); (b) generates individual employee contribution certificates on request (e.g., for SSS salary loan application, Pag-IBIG housing loan application); (c) annual: reconcile total contributions against each agency&#x27;s annual statement of account
Responsible (R): Payroll Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1527_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1527_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1527_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1527_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1527_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-297 (ensure controlled execution — Payroll &amp; Compensation (PA-19.2).) | - operational: Payroll Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Payroll Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1527_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1527_Annotation13" targetRef="W1527_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1527_Flow15" sourceRef="W1527_Start5" targetRef="W1527_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1527_Flow16" sourceRef="W1527_Task6" targetRef="W1527_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1527_Flow17" sourceRef="W1527_Task7" targetRef="W1527_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1527_Flow18" sourceRef="W1527_Task8" targetRef="W1527_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1527_Flow19" sourceRef="W1527_Task9" targetRef="W1527_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1527_Flow20" sourceRef="W1527_Task10" targetRef="W1527_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1527_Flow21" sourceRef="W1527_Task11" targetRef="W1527_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1527_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1527_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1527">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1527_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1527_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1527_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1527_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1527_Lane3_di" bpmnElement="W1527_Lane3" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="420" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1527_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1527_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1527_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1527_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1527_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1527_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1527_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W1527_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="465" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1527_Task10_di" bpmnElement="W1527_Task10"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1527_Task11_di" bpmnElement="W1527_Task11"><dc:Bounds x="1450" y="465" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1527_Start5_di" bpmnElement="W1527_Start5"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1527_End12_di" bpmnElement="W1527_End12"><dc:Bounds x="1680" y="487" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1527_Annotation13_di" bpmnElement="W1527_Annotation13"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="630" width="360" height="72" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1527_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1527_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1527_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1527_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1527_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W1527_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="790" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1527_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W1527_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1527_Flow19_di" bpmnElement="W1527_Flow19"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="505" /><di:waypoint x="1240" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1527_Flow20_di" bpmnElement="W1527_Flow20"><di:waypoint x="1420" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1450" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1527_Flow21_di" bpmnElement="W1527_Flow21"><di:waypoint x="1630" y="505" /><di:waypoint x="1680" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1527_Assoc14_di" bpmnElement="W1527_Assoc14"><di:waypoint x="340" y="630" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W5540" name="W5540. Payroll Run Failure, Correction &amp; Emergency Off-Cycle Payment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: A payroll run aborts or is compromised inside the payroll window: validation failure on the payroll register, bank-file (credit/debit-advice) rejection by the disbursement bank, funding shortblock, payroll-system/ERP outage at cut-off, or a disbursement-partner platform outage
Frequency: ~2–6 failure events chain-wide per year across the 6,911-employee estate (monthly run × 5 entities; most aborts caught at validation and re-run inside the window)
Volume: 1 run × affected population (a validation abort typically hits 1–3 batches; a bank-file reject or provider outage hits up to all ~6,911 payslips for that entity-run) × statutory remittance deadlines (W1527/W1306) that keep running regardless
Owner: Payroll Manager
Participants: Payroll Specialist, HR Shared Services (employee comms per VS-103), Finance Controller (funding release), Treasury (funding/debit account status per VS-18), IT Service Desk &amp; ERP payroll support (system restoration), disbursement bank / payroll funding partner, CHRO (communications), HR Benefits (SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG desk), Audit (post-mortem for material events)
Source: workflow W5540 — Payroll Run Failure, Correction &amp; Emergency Off-Cycle Payment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5540_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5540_Lane1" name="Payroll Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5540_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5540_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5540_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5540_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5540_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5540_Lane2" name="Payroll Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5540_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5540_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5540_Lane3" name="HR Shared Services">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5540_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5540_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5540_Start5" name="A payroll run aborts or is compromised inside the payroll window: validation failure on…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5540_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5540_Task6" name="Failure classification &amp; clock">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Failure classification &amp; clock: classify against the payday countdown — (a) validation abort ≥ 48 h before payday → correct &amp; re-run (Step 2); (b) bank-file rejection / provider outage &lt; 48 h → contingency branch (Steps 3–5); (c) funding block (Treasury/debit account issue) → Treasury joint branch (Step 3c); open the event log with timestamps (recovery-time accountability)
Responsible (R): Payroll Specialist
Accountable (A): Payroll Manager
Duration: 30–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5540_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5540_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5540_Task7" name="Correct &amp; re-run (inside window)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Correct &amp; re-run (inside window): isolate failing records (negative net, invalid deduction, missing bank/enrollment per W10 validations), fix master-data or deduction errors, re-run only the failed batches with the normal approval chain intact (CTL-13: computation/approval separation preserved under time pressure); confirm register-to-bank-file control totals
Responsible (R): Payroll Specialist / Payroll Manager
Accountable (A): Payroll Manager
Duration: 2–6 hrs</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5540_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5540_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5540_Task8" name="Funding &amp; file verification (contingency branch)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Funding &amp; file verification (contingency branch): (a) bank-file reject → obtain the bank&#x27;s reject/error report, regenerate the file per spec, resubmit and obtain acknowledged credit-advice; (b) provider platform outage → invoke the secondary disbursement channel per contract (backup partner or alternate file protocol); (c) funding block → Treasury confirms debit-account funding per the W318 settlement-account structure and releases per Finance Controller sign-off
Responsible (R): Payroll Specialist / Treasury / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 2–12 hrs</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5540_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5540_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5540_Task9" name="Emergency off-cycle payment decision (&lt; 24 h to payday, credit not assured)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Emergency off-cycle payment decision (&lt; 24 h to payday, credit not assured): CHRO + Finance Controller approve an emergency net-pay advance via the W641 off-cycle rails — scope: affected employees, amount (default 50% net, up to 100% for hardship cases), channel (card-partner push or store cash-card load for cash-paid segments under dual-custody cash controls per VS-81 store-cash rules); employees sign the W641 advance agreement (recovery via deduction from the late-arriving original credit)
Responsible (R): Payroll Manager / CHRO / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CHRO + Finance Controller (joint)
Duration: 4–8 hrs</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5540_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5540_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5540_Task10" name="Employee communication &amp; floor support">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Employee communication &amp; floor support: HR Shared Services issues the ESS banner + SMS/email with facts, cause, and the assured new credit time; store/DC bulletins via the VS-63 store-communication channel; payroll helpdesk surge script (no-pay-confirmation handling); store managers briefed not to improvise promises
Responsible (R): HR Shared Services / Store Managers
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 2–4 hrs</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5540_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5540_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5540_Task11" name="Statutory protection &amp; reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Statutory protection &amp; reconciliation: verify remittance calendar still met — SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG (W1527) and BIR withholding (W1306 chain) computed from the corrected register, paid on statutory deadlines with penalty exposure assessed if the failure touches them; when the original credit lands late, reconcile against any Step-4 advances (deduction per agreement), close the register-to-bank reconciliation, and document the event trail for audit
Responsible (R): Payroll Specialist / HR Benefits
Accountable (A): Payroll Manager
Duration: 4–16 hrs</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5540_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5540_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5540_Task12" name="Post-mortem &amp; control hardening">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Post-mortem &amp; control hardening: within 5 business days — root cause (data, file spec, funding, vendor, infrastructure), run-book update, added pre-run validations, provider SLA review or channel remediation; material events (full-run failure, &gt; 24 h delay, statutory penalty) reported to the Audit Committee via the W81-class write-off/exception reporting path if losses resulted
Responsible (R): Payroll Manager / Audit
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5540_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5540_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5540_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5540_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5540_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-297 (ensure controlled execution — Payroll &amp; Compensation (PA-19.2).); CTL-13 (separate payroll computation from approval.); CTL-34 (ensure complete tax compliance.) | - operational: emergency advances ride W641 agreements with documented recovery deductions — never free-standing payouts | - operational: every failure event carries a timestamped event log and a 5-day post-mortem with control-hardening actions
Owner: Payroll Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
